# In VR the desktop window's focus changes nothing in the game (#406): the player in the headset does not see the
# window, and clicking OBS, a browser or Discord takes its focus (streaming and recording, #576/#77). A focus loss and
# its return during gameplay keep free look (no cursor mode: the inventory stays shut, melee is not refused), keep the
# combat mode, and the game keeps running - frames, the game clock, the headset session. The flat counterpart, where a
# focus loss still leaves free look and puts the weapon away: the end of desktop-mouse-flat.xrs.
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence window-focus -Save mvp-goblin-fight
#
# The test channel's command this sequence needs (written before the implementation, #406):
#   window focus lost | window focus gained
#       the game window losing / getting the input focus, as when the player clicks another program or back on the
#       game: SDL_WINDOWEVENT_FOCUS_LOST / SDL_WINDOWEVENT_FOCUS_GAINED for the game window pushed into SDL's event
#       queue (as desktop-mouse does for the mouse), so it reaches the game through the same path as the real event -
#       SDL2Window's event loop, Window::onFocus, ArxGame::onWindowLostFocus / onWindowGotFocus. Not a flag set beside
#       it: status.json window.focused follows it (Window::hasFocus), and flat mode must react to it as to a real one.
#       The existing "window <width> <height>" stays as it is.
# Status fields read (all exist): window.focused, player.freelook, player.inventoryOpen, player.bookOpen,
# vr.weapon.combatMode, vr.melee.*, frame, vr.frames, gameTimeMs, paused, vr.sessionState.
# The CI runner's window is never activated (window.focused false from the start, #487), so the focus is given first:
# the loss below is a real change.
@sim idle
@save mvp-goblin-fight
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert player.freelook eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
# A touch is the minimum (the default, set live: a cfg.ini of an earlier build may keep another value, TRAPS.md)
melee noswing min

# The goblin held still 80 units ahead, the sword level with its chest, the hand to the right - moved there slowly
# (0.43 m in 60 frames: under 0.7 m/s, no swing), as in melee-swing.xrs
goblin_base_0036.setspeed 0
place goblin_base_0036 80
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
vr-sim head rot 0 -25 0
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0

# 1. The window gets the focus: nothing changes in the game
window focus gained
@until window.focused eq true 5s
@frames 10
@assert player.freelook eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
@assert vr.melee.active eq true

# 2. The window loses the focus (the player clicked another program): still free look, the inventory and the book shut,
# melee not refused, and the game runs on - frames drawn and sent to the headset, the game clock, no pause
window focus lost
@until window.focused eq false 5s
@remember frame0 frame
@remember vrFrames0 vr.frames
@remember clock0 gameTimeMs
@wait 1000
@assert player.freelook eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
@assert player.bookOpen eq false
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
@assert paused eq false
@assert vr.sessionState eq focused
@assert frame ge {frame0+20}
@assert vr.frames ge {vrFrames0+20}
@assert gameTimeMs ge {clock0+500}

# 3. Melee works while the window has no focus: a fast swing through the goblin (0.85 m in 8 frames) hits it
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 1 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.hits eq {hits+1}
@assert vr.melee.last.target eq goblin_base_0036
@assert window.focused eq false

# 4. The focus comes back: the same - free look, the inventory shut, a swing back still hits
window focus gained
@until window.focused eq true 5s
@frames 30
@assert player.freelook eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 2 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.hits eq {hits+1}

# 5. The combat mode survives a focus loss and its return (the engine's handler turned it off)
combat on
@until vr.weapon.combatMode eq true 5s
window focus lost
@until window.focused eq false 5s
@frames 30
@assert vr.weapon.combatMode eq true
@assert player.freelook eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
window focus gained
@until window.focused eq true 5s
@frames 30
@assert vr.weapon.combatMode eq true
@assert player.freelook eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
combat off
@until vr.weapon.combatMode eq false 5s

@assert errors eq 0
